From 892a5a061a8cf486acb45985b8ff40383a73241c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:02:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban placement: no worker-first card that no pool
 worker can claim

Two MacBook cards (t_01a1d5386cb55abf, t_01a1d54acc8c8e54, 11-13 14:03Z/14:23Z) sat
ready 42 and 22 min with 140 and 49 reservations across worker-2..4 and were never
claimed until their bodies were edited.

Five whys:
1. queue_decision returned None: coordination.required_labels() was None.
2. requirements() matched `hermes-hub tasks` in the body's "## Existing work
   checked" record ("On 11-13 at 06:05 PST, `hermes-hub tasks` (all boards) had no
   open card ..."), a past search, as a home coordination action.
3. creation_decision then fell back to worker-first-v1 from the MacBook's stale
   worker_pools list (worker-2..4) without re-checking the coordination refusal.
4. Every reserved worker's claim_refusal re-ran the same scan and refused, so the
   origin re-reserved it every tick (the comment flood t_01a1d54acc8c8e54 reports).
5. Nothing marked the record ask-gate's superseding_work rule asks for as evidence,
   and nothing kept a worker_queue gateway's queue miss out of worker-first.
   Third recurrence of the class (hermes-hub's, hermes-hub outcomes, now tasks).

Fix:
- without_evidence() also strips an "Existing work checked" heading section (to
  the next heading) or bold-label paragraph (to the next blank line). It feeds the
  portability scan, required_labels and claim_refusal alike.
- creation_decision never enrolls worker-first on a gateway with a worker_queue
  label: a queue miss (no live labelled machine, non-primary board) stays home
  under legacy routing.
- creation_decision never enrolls a card whose required_labels is None (claim_refusal
  refuses it on every pool worker), matching the hub-admission deny path.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_existing_work_checked.py RED 10 failed / 2
passed (controls) on the unpatched source, GREEN 12 passed. The 79 test files
naming kanban_worker_placement / worker-first / without_evidence / worker_pools:
1988 passed, 1 failed = test_direct_create_task_keeps_pool_enrollment_when_it_cannot_queue,
which encoded the retired fallback; rewritten to the new contract (and to keep
enrollment on a gateway without a queue).

Card: t_01a1d55f5bbdae39
